    "## Task 1 — Graph Design\n",
    "\n",
    "### State schema\n",
    "\n",
    "The shared state contains:\n",
    "- `user_query`: current user message\n",
    "- `conversation_history`: previous turns\n",
    "- `intent`: `factual`, `retrieval`, `prediction`, or `off-topic`\n",
    "- `tool_results`: outputs/errors from retrieval or prediction tools\n",
    "- `final_response`: formatted answer\n",
    "- extra routing fields for validation, clarification, and trace logging\n",
    "\n",
    "### Graph\n",
    "\n",
    "`START → router → {direct_answer | retrieval_tool | prediction_tool | refusal}`\n",
    "\n",
    "`retrieval_tool / prediction_tool → validation → {response_formatter | clarification | fallback}`\n",
    "\n",
    "`direct_answer / refusal / clarification / fallback → response_formatter → END`\n",
    "\n",
    "Explicit routing is safer than a single free-form agent because each intent has a controlled path. Prediction requests always pass through the prediction node and validation/formatting logic, so the application can consistently include probabilities, grounding features, and uncertainty language instead of allowing a generic agent to produce an unsupported certainty claim.\n"
   ]
  },
