   "source": [
    "## Task 5 — Comparison with a monolithic LangChain agent\n",
    "\n",
    "A single monolithic agent has to decide both **what** to do and **how** to respond, which increases the chance of choosing the wrong tool or inventing a result when an entity is ambiguous. LangGraph makes the control flow explicit: prediction, retrieval, validation, clarification, fallback, and response formatting are separate nodes, so prediction requests consistently pass through probability/grounding rules and invalid tool results cannot silently become confident answers.\n"
   ]
  },
